E7 - does the LAG survival survive it too? (REG-002 E7, registered before coding)
==============================================================================
  Section 4.5 reports the lag ordering holding in 100% of 400 random admissible
  ladders -- drawn under the SAME two constraints E1 drops. If the statistic that
  survived the confound survived it only because of the durability assumption,
  section 4.5's concession needs narrowing in the same breath it reports the 100%.

  lag non-decreasing up the ladder, ORDERED delta   : 100.0%   (WT-083 reports 100.0%)
  lag non-decreasing up the ladder, UNORDERED delta : 69.0%
  compare the MAGNITUDE measure, unordered          : 11.5%
  binomial se at M = 400 (WT-083's sample size, the registered one) : 0.023

  PRECISION CHECK, same estimator at M = 2000                       : 66.2%  (se 0.011)
  the registered figure sits 0.43 se from the registered
  threshold; the precision check sits 3.55 se from it.

  REG-002 E7: below 0.70 -> narrow the concession; at or above 0.90 ->
  a strengthening obtained by trying to break it.
  registered M = 400: 0.690   ·   precision M = 2000: 0.662
  -> NARROW
  SEVERE     the lag ordering DEGRADES materially once the durability ordering is dropped
  Witness is the ordered draw asked to fall materially below itself.
  SEVERE     the timing statistic survives an assumption the magnitude statistic needed
  Witness is the magnitude measure asked to clear its own bar, which it cannot.

